    <statement><p>Suppose that the line <m>\ell</m> is represented by <m>\mathbf{r}(t) = \langle 9+2 t, 12+4 t, 5+ 2 t \rangle</m> and the plane <m>P</m> is represented by <m>3x-2y+5z = 8.</m></p>
<p><alert> 1. </alert> Find the intersection of the line <m>\ell</m> and the plane <m>P.</m> <alert> Write your answer as a point <m>(a,b,c)</m> where <m>a</m>, <m>b</m>, and <m>c</m> are numbers. </alert></p>
<p>Answer: <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p><alert> 2. </alert> Find the cosine of the angle <m>\theta</m> between the line <m>\ell</m> and the normal vector of the plane <m>P</m>.</p>
<p>Answer: <m>\cos \theta =</m> <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p><alert> Note: </alert> <em> If there is no intersection, write "none" for both answers.</em></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\left(4,2,0\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{2\cdot 3+4\cdot \left(-2\right)+2\cdot 5}{\sqrt{2^{2}+4^{2}+2^{2}}\sqrt{3^{2}+\left(-2\right)^{2}+5^{2}}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
